(2292, 'App\\Models\\Product', '65d4f61147736-prod-85301799523742276', 'en', 'key_features', '<p style=\"color: rgb(82, 89, 111); font-family: Jost, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.024px; background-color: rgb(247, 247, 248); margin-block: 0px 0.9rem;\">Pull-down workholding clamps generate pull-down action, pressing workpieces down onto the fixture base, as an alternative to applying sideways force to the jaw on the fixture base.</p><p style=\"color: rgb(82, 89, 111); font-family: Jost, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.024px; background-color: rgb(247, 247, 248); margin-block: 0px 0.9rem;\">The OK Vise single-wedge pull-down clamp design is a standard single-wedge clamp (inverted ) and combined with a pull-down set (a combination of a plate and a bushing).</p><p style=\"color: rgb(82, 89, 111); font-family: Jost, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.024px; background-color: rgb(247, 247, 248); margin-block: 0px 0.9rem;\">The major differences of single-wedge pull-down clamp when compared with double wedge pull-down clamps are :</p><ul style=\"color: rgb(82, 89, 111); font-family: Jost, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.024px; background: rgb(247, 247, 248); margin-block: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; vertical-align: baseline;\"><li style=\"margin-block: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">There are more variations of jaw types and clamp sizes.</li><li style=\"margin-block: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">The angle of the movement is steeper.</li><li style=\"margin-block: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">It is easy to test fixture with and without pull-down property.</li></ul>', '2024-02-21 01:57:21', '2024-02-21 01:57:21'),
(2293, 'App\\Models\\Product', '65d4f61147736-prod-85301799523742276', 'en', 'further_information', '<p><br></p>', '2024-02-21 01:57:21', '2024-02-21 01:57:21'),
(2294, 'App\\Models\\Product', '65d4fbf9c56af-prod-75829819017526029', 'en', 'name', 'OK-Vise Single Wedge Pull Down Model', '2024-02-21 02:22:33', '2024-02-21 02:22:33'),
(2295, 'App\\Models\\Product', '65d4fbf9c56af-prod-75829819017526029', 'en', 'key_features', '<p style=\"color: rgb(82, 89, 111); font-family: Jost, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.024px; background-color: rgb(247, 247, 248); margin-block: 0px 0.9rem;\">Pull-down workholding clamps generate pull-down action, pressing workpieces down onto the fixture base, as an alternative to applying sideways force to the jaw on the fixture base.</p><p style=\"color: rgb(82, 89, 111); font-family: Jost, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.024px; background-color: rgb(247, 247, 248); margin-block: 0px 0.9rem;\">The OK Vise single-wedge pull-down clamp design is a standard single-wedge clamp (inverted ) and combined with a pull-down set (a combination of a plate and a bushing).</p><p style=\"color: rgb(82, 89, 111); font-family: Jost, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.024px; background-color: rgb(247, 247, 248); margin-block: 0px 0.9rem;\">The major differences of single-wedge pull-down clamp when compared with double wedge pull-down clamps are :</p><ul style=\"color: rgb(82, 89, 111); font-family: Jost, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.024px; background: rgb(247, 247, 248); margin-block: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; vertical-align: baseline;\"><li style=\"margin-block: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">There are more variations of jaw types and clamp sizes.</li><li style=\"margin-block: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">The angle of the movement is steeper.</li><li style=\"margin-block: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">It is easy to test fixture with and without pull-down property.</li></ul>', '2024-02-21 02:22:33', '2024-02-21 02:22:33'),
(2296, 'App\\Models\\Product', '65d4fbf9c56af-prod-75829819017526029', 'en', 'further_information', '<p><br></p>', '2024-02-21 02:22:33', '2024-02-21 02:22:33'),
(2297, 'App\\Models\\Product', '65d4feafd28b0-prod-34611754282564878', 'en', 'name', 'OK-Vise Single Wedge Pull Down Model', '2024-02-21 02:34:07', '2024-02-21 02:34:07'),
(2298, 'App\\Models\\Product', '65d4feafd28b0-prod-34611754282564878', 'en', 'key_features', '<p style=\"color: rgb(82, 89, 111); font-family: Jost, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.024px; background-color: rgb(247, 247, 248); margin-block: 0px 0.9rem;\">Pull-down workholding clamps generate pull-down action, pressing workpieces down onto the fixture base, as an alternative to applying sideways force to the jaw on the fixture base.</p><p style=\"color: rgb(82, 89, 111); font-family: Jost, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.024px; background-color: rgb(247, 247, 248); margin-block: 0px 0.9rem;\">The OK Vise single-wedge pull-down clamp design is a standard single-wedge clamp (inverted ) and combined with a pull-down set (a combination of a plate and a bushing).</p><p style=\"color: rgb(82, 89, 111); font-family: Jost, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.024px; background-color: rgb(247, 247, 248); margin-block: 0px 0.9rem;\">The major differences of single-wedge pull-down clamp when compared with double wedge pull-down clamps are :</p><ul style=\"color: rgb(82, 89, 111); font-family: Jost, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.024px; background: rgb(247, 247, 248); margin-block: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; vertical-align: baseline;\"><li style=\"margin-block: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">There are more variations of jaw types and clamp sizes.</li><li style=\"margin-block: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">The angle of the movement is steeper.</li><li style=\"margin-block: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">It is easy to test fixture with and without pull-down property.</li></ul>', '2024-02-21 02:34:07', '2024-02-21 02:34:07'),
(2299, 'App\\Models\\Product', '65d4feafd28b0-prod-34611754282564878', 'en', 'further_information', '<p><br></p>', '2024-02-21 02:34:07', '2024-02-21 02:34:07'),
(2300, 'App\\Models\\Category', '65d5050305277-ctgr-88645933844153656', 'en', 'title', 'Double Wedge Pull Down Model', '2024-02-21 03:01:07', '2024-02-21 03:01:07'),
(2301, 'App\\Models\\Product', '65d507d402693-prod-57855113194112347', 'en', 'name', 'OK-Vise Double Wedge Pull Down Model', '2024-02-21 03:13:08', '2024-02-21 03:13:08'),
(2302, 'App\\Models\\Product', '65d507d402693-prod-57855113194112347', 'en', 'key_features', '<p style=\"margin-block: 0px 0.9rem;\">Pull-down workholding clamps generate pull-down action pressing workpieces down onto the fixture base, as an alternative to applying sideways force to the jaw on the fixture base.</p><p style=\"margin-block: 0px 0.9rem;\">The double-wedge pull-down clamp is the most traditional model. It is available with both a serrated and smooth jaw option.</p><p style=\"margin-block: 0px 0.9rem;\">Whilst single-wedge clamps keep workpieces tight in one place, preventing upward and downward movement the double-wedge clamps generate a pull-down effect, pressing the workpieces downwards onto the fixture base.</p><p style=\"margin-block: 0px 0.9rem;\">The F-size model with its extreme clamping force of 150 kN is the strongest model in our range of low-profile clamps.</p>', '2024-02-21 03:13:08', '2024-02-21 03:13:08'),
(2303, 'App\\Models\\Product', '65d507d402693-prod-57855113194112347', 'en', 'further_information', '<p><br></p>', '2024-02-21 03:13:08', '2024-02-21 03:13:08'),
